Package: kelixip-mod-dialog-state
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.ives.fr/
Depends: kelixip (= @VERSION@), kelixip-mod-presence (= @VERSION@)
Description: Call occupancy of the served users, for kelixip
 The call state of each served user, reported to the presence collection: a
 BLF key subscribed with Event: dialog (RFC 4235) lights while its user rings
 or talks, a presence watcher sees on-the-phone while a call is up, and an ACD
 is pushed every transition. Only a call whose party is proven a user of the
 domain counts: authenticated by digest, or reached through its
 registrations. Enable it with a [module.dialog_state] block in config.toml,
 next to [module.presence].
 .
 The payload is BEAM bytecode, but the package is architecture-dependent on
 purpose: it must be built and shipped alongside the core whose embedded ERTS
 will load it.
